Implement the remaining G2 functional instructions (DG-004d), spec-derived
(§3.14/§4.7 block copy, §5 control flow), never from QEMU translate.c.

registers.hh: add the RegRAS bank ra0..ra63 (int class 128..191); NumIntRegs
128 → 192. RA is architectural but internal (not an operand), accessed by
call/ret via ThreadContext.

decoder.cc:
  - Conditional branches br{n,nn,z,nz,p,np} (riii §5.1) / br{eq,ne} (rrii §5.2):
    condition per Appendix B on rdha (rd0→0); taken PC ← (PC+4 + sext<<2) mod
    2^48, else fall through.
  - jump_r (rrii §5.3): target = base + rdhb + sext12<<2; rbha=rb0 ⇒ relative.
  - call_i (iiii §5.4) / call_r (rrii §5.4): push rb0(=PC+4) to RegRAS, jump.
  - ret (riii §5.5): pop RegRAS → PC; rdha = sext18(imms18).
  - RegRAS push/pop (§5.6) mirrors the spec's refcount/shift model; RASOF (full)
    / RASUF (empty) are precise (PC & RA unchanged).
  - Register block copy rd2rd/rd2rb/rb2rd/rb2rb (§3.14/§4.7): copy immu6 regs;
    asymmetry — RB *source* reads low 48 bits (rb2rd/rb2rb dest high16=0), RD
    source reads full 64, dest written full width (rd2rb stores 64). Legality
    (immu6=0 / dest reg0 / src|dst+immu6>64) → ILLI.

faults.hh: RasofFault(0x84)/RasufFault(0x85) (untested by runnable vectors; the
cold-ret abstain is HARNESS).

3-way differential: AGREE(3-way) 162 → 198, DIVERGE=0, gem5-SKIP=0 — gem5 now
covers ALL 198 interp+QEMU-agreed cases. The 6 HARNESS control-flow abstains
(jump/call/ret rb0=0, cold-RAS ret — trampoline artifacts) remain out of scope.
Smokes 42/42/0. G2 = functional second reference achieved.

